From: Local Z96A hardware validation
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: z96a: expose the GPIO0_B7 status LED

The factory Z96A device tree describes exactly one extra LED besides the
charging indicators: a status ("work") LED on GPIO0_B7, active low, driven
by the heartbeat trigger.  The mainline Z96A DTS instead claimed GPIO0_B7
as the Bluetooth host-wake line, so the LED could never be driven.  The
factory firmware uses GPIO0_C4 for both the WiFi and Bluetooth host wake,
so the host-wake property is simply dropped here; the three-wire HCI data
path never used it.

Expose the LED as /sys/class/leds/white:status.  It has no dedicated
function on this board, so userspace can repurpose it, for example as the
microphone mute indicator (see z96a-hotkey).

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-sunniwell-z96a-typec.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-sunniwell-z96a-typec.dts
@@ -156,6 +156,20 @@
 
 	leds {
 		compatible = "gpio-leds";
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&work_led_pin>;
+
+		/*
+		 * Status LED on GPIO0_B7, active low.  The factory firmware drives
+		 * it with the heartbeat trigger; it is the only LED that has no
+		 * dedicated function, so userspace may repurpose it.
+		 */
+		led_work: led-work {
+			gpios = <&gpio0 RK_PB7 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+			function = LED_FUNCTION_STATUS;
+			color = <LED_COLOR_ID_WHITE>;
+			linux,default-trigger = "heartbeat";
+		};
 
 		led_power: led-power {
 			gpios = <&gpio0 RK_PD3 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
@@ -860,7 +874,7 @@
 		bt_enable_h: bt-enable-h {
 			rockchip,pins = <0 RK_PC1 RK_FUNC_GPIO &pcfg_pull_none>;
 		};
-		bt_host_wake: bt-host-wake {
+		work_led_pin: work-led-pin {
 			rockchip,pins = <0 RK_PB7 RK_FUNC_GPIO &pcfg_pull_none>;
 		};
 		bt_wake: bt-wake {
@@ -948,9 +962,8 @@
 		compatible = "realtek,rtl8822cs-bt";
 		enable-gpios = <&gpio0 RK_PC1 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		device-wake-gpios = <&gpio0 RK_PB0 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
-		host-wake-gpios = <&gpio0 RK_PB7 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
-		pinctrl-0 = <&bt_enable_h &bt_host_wake &bt_wake>;
+		pinctrl-0 = <&bt_enable_h &bt_wake>;
 	};
 };
 
